From 10aff024b1d395c8b72c95872ea06a5a2a8a85b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 15:24:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Test item 3-1's remaining populations, and void 0108's
 ranking with them

0110 voided 0108's consumer-side refusals of PropertyRead, CallResult
and NeverOffered by establishing that the bound was on a different
quantity. Two of the three are expressible as assumptions and are
measured here by 0110's method: build the representation behind a flag,
read boxingSpeculativeReadRequests before anything else.

                cost (specReads)   saving (roots)   requests  allocated
  Parameter               417 582         -304 372      1.003      1.006
  PropertyRead          3 828 813           72 980      1.030      1.045
  CallResult              913 011          431 131      1.004      1.006

All three refuted. Every population costs more than it saves, which is
now four of four tried.

And 0108's bound was not merely low, it was uncorrelated. It predicted
CallResult 9.41 and PropertyRead 1.83, ranking CallResult as the worst
of the two by five times. Measured, PropertyRead is 52.5 and CallResult
2.12 -- the reverse, by twenty-five times. A bound taken at the wrong
sites does not preserve the ordering of the quantity it is standing in
for, which is a stronger statement than 0110 could make from one
population.

NavierStokes mints exactly 393 705 speculative-read boxes under
CallResult, the same figure it mints under Parameter and the same one
this document records for item 3-8a. Three populations, one number: on
the suite that decides these items they are the same handful of names
reached by different assumptions.

NeverOffered is not testable by this method and the reason is
structural, not effort. The cause means the DECLARATION is non-numeric
-- `var a = []`, `var s = ''` -- so there is no assumption about a value
source that admits it; the fixed point drops it on its own initializer.
Holding it speculatively is not a widening of the analysis but a
decision to represent every non-numeric local speculatively, which is a
different proposition. Its ceiling is 241 567 boxed writes, 1.5% of the
16.4 M, against costs between 0.4 M and 3.8 M on every population
measured -- so it is argued rather than measured, and labelled as such.

8 176 tests with all switches off and 1 294 compiler tests with the two
new ones forced on.
